445	461,878,832,1679 - 461,1200,548,1352 - 815,1280,832,1679	445. Branch of Forget-me-not, in flower.	A leafy branch of Forget-me-not: small five-lobed flowers with a ring at the centre crowded at the coiled tip, and older flowers on spreading pedicels below.
446	267,1203,543,1348	446. The corolla laid open, with the stamens, magnified.	The Forget-me-not corolla slit and spread flat, magnified: five rounded lobes above a short tube, with the stamens and small scales standing in a row inside.
447	357,1391,461,1641	447. The pistil with its 4-lobed ovary; calyx, &c. cut away.	The Forget-me-not pistil, the calyx cut away: four round lobes of the ovary seated together, with the single style rising from between them.
448	136,1372,318,1635	448. Two of the ripe akenes in the calyx; the two sepals towards the eye and two of the akenes removed.	The calyx opened to show two ripe akenes standing upright inside, with pointed sepals rising behind them.
449	136,1197,228,1333	449. Akene cut through lengthwise, magnified; the whole kernel embryo.	A single akene cut through lengthwise and magnified: an egg-shaped outline with a smooth kernel filling the inside.
450	824,1291,1105,1660	450. Flowers of Comfrey.	A drooping cluster of Comfrey flowers: tubular, bell-like corollas hanging from a curved stalk, with buds at the tip.
451	870,948,1140,1092	451. Corolla enlarged, laid open, showing the sharp scales inside, and the stamens.	A Comfrey corolla enlarged and laid open: a scalloped tube with a row of sharp, pointed scales between the stamens inside.
